WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:03.241
Easy Greek Myths. Theseus and the Minotaur.

00:00:03.241 --> 00:00:06.706
On the island of Crete there lived a terrible monster.

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:10.036
It had the body of a man and the head of a bull.

00:00:10.036 --> 00:00:11.936
It was called the Minotaur.

00:00:11.936 --> 00:00:17.310
The king of Crete kept it in a huge building full of paths that turned and crossed.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:20.358
Nobody who went in could find the way out again.

00:00:20.358 --> 00:00:26.564
Every year, the city of Athens had to send seven young men and seven young women to Crete.

00:00:26.564 --> 00:00:30.236
They were sent into the building, and the monster ate them.

00:00:30.236 --> 00:00:33.212
Theseus was the son of the king of Athens.

00:00:33.212 --> 00:00:37.929
"I will go as one of the seven," he said, "and I will kill the monster."

00:00:37.929 --> 00:00:43.325
When Theseus arrived in Crete, the king's daughter, Ariadne, saw him.

00:00:43.325 --> 00:00:46.281
She fell in love with him and decided to help.

00:00:46.281 --> 00:00:48.814
That night she came to him in secret.

00:00:48.814 --> 00:00:51.700
She gave him a sword and a ball of string.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:55.208
"Tie the end of the string to the door," she said.

00:00:55.208 --> 00:00:56.959
"Let it out as you walk.

00:00:56.959 --> 00:00:58.922
Then you can follow it back."

00:00:58.922 --> 00:01:00.964
Theseus did as she said.

00:01:00.964 --> 00:01:04.049
He walked deeper and deeper into the dark building.

00:01:04.049 --> 00:01:06.535
At last he heard heavy breathing.

00:01:06.535 --> 00:01:08.489
The Minotaur ran at him.

00:01:08.489 --> 00:01:10.682
They fought for a long time.

00:01:10.682 --> 00:01:14.205
In the end Theseus killed the monster with his sword.

00:01:14.205 --> 00:01:19.802
Then he picked up the string and followed it, turn after turn, back to the door.

00:01:19.802 --> 00:01:21.483
Ariadne was waiting.

00:01:21.483 --> 00:01:27.462
Together with the other young people, they ran to the ship and sailed away before the king woke up.

00:01:27.462 --> 00:01:30.914
Athens never had to send its children to Crete again.
